## History and archive boundary

The Dashboard separates current guidance and work from project history and inactive material. Do not load history or archive documents during normal work unless the task needs past evidence, reuse, or restoration.

When a major delivery version or working method changes and prior detailed progress would mislead current work, copy the superseded material into a dated or stable archive package under `99_archive`, keep a concise restoration pointer in the active record, and preserve the source unless a separate approved action changes it. A standard package contains bilingual archive notes and `ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.json` with payload closure and an inventory fingerprint.

