## Review style

- Keep documents concise and factual.
- Separate current, retired, proposed, and unknown states.
- Separate lifecycle from evidence authority; retained material may exist without current decision authority.
- Keep volatile counts and execution snapshots in dated logs or registries, not repeated across durable files.
- Link to real paths instead of copying large outputs.
- Record why a fact is believed and when it stops being valid.
- Use HTML `<strong>...</strong>` for bold text. Do not author Markdown `**...**`; inline code, fenced code, and glob paths retain literal asterisks.
